BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Delicious and Surprising History of The Dining Room
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261214T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261214T200000
UID:6aa0836a4cb69d003e26ac6f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:John Ota presents​ and discusses his book\,\nThe Dining Room
  : Exploring the Design of Twelve Iconic Rooms in Search of the Perfect Di
 ning Experience.​\n​(Random House\, 2026).\nExplore the stories behind
  twelve iconic dining rooms in homes around the world—from a Japanese sa
 murai house to Claude Monet's brilliant yellow dining room to Frida Kahlo'
 s Casa Azul to Jackie Kennedy’s White House—and travel through time in
  pursuit of the ultimate design.​
LOCATION:St. Lawrence\, Ground Floor\, South Side
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa0836a4cb69d003e26ac6f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
