DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261023T150000
UID:6aa700084b3b060030837a37@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to make environmentally-friendly\, recycled\, handma
 de paper in this fun\, easy\, and interactive workshop. Leave with sheets 
 of beautiful\, one-of-a-kind paper plus the knowledge that you did somethi
 ng great for the earth!\nParticipants will learn about the ancient craft o
 f papermaking\, and have an opportunity to make their own beautiful\, recy
 cled paper from paper scraps\, plus a variety of techniques to further cus
 tomize their sheets.\nRegistration required.\nInformation Collection Notic
 e:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Publ
 ic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 2
 0(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration
 \, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your i
 nformation can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-
 397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Beaches\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa700084b3b060030837a37
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
