DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261026T190000
UID:6aaa95de129d8e0031f2a2ce@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Find out what it takes to be a young entrepreneur\, hear some 
 Canadian success stories\, and share ideas of your own in an inclusive and
  supportive space! Plus\, find out more about all the great resources in p
 lace across Canada to support young entrepreneurs\, and how you can access
  funding\, mentoring and learning opportunities no matter where you live.\
 nRegistration required. Limited spots. Young Adults (ages 18-24) have prio
 rity for this workshop.\nThis program will be taking place in the\nFounder
 's Room\n\, located on the first floor (past the staircase\, down the hal
 lway to the right).\n----\nThis workshop is part of the Youth for Entrepre
 neurship program led by the YMCA of Greater Toronto. Through hands-on sess
 ions\, you’ll gain the digital tools\, financial knowledge\, and creativ
 e strategies needed to build a business idea from the ground up.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Founder's Room (1st Floor)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaa95de129d8e0031f2a2ce
