UID:6a1f48e0c7d3cd58005d9831@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:LivingWorks SafeTALK\nis a half-day workshop that prepares par
 ticipants to recognize when someone might be having thoughts of suicide an
 d how to connect them to life-saving support. Learn practical skills to h
 elp someone keep safe and guide them toward further help.\nWho should atte
 nd?\nIndividuals aged 15 and up\nPeople who want to support suicide safety
  in their community\nNo previous training or experience is required. All 
 participants will receive a\nLivingWorks SafeTALK certificate\nupon worksh
 op completion.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGerstein Crisis Cen
 tre’s SafeTALK initiative\n.\nGerstein Crisis Centre is solely responsib
 le for the protection of personal information collected through the progra
 m registration process.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, Children's Program Room - First floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1f48e0c7d3cd58005d9831
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
