BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Works by Sine Lam
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261001T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261031T235959
UID:6a80ca5ebe1482002987994a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of October\, works by artist Sine Lam wil
 l be on display at the Forest Hill branch.\nSine Lam is an emerging artist
  currently based in Ontario. She studied Fine Art at St. Lawrence College.
  Her artistic practice blends symbolism\, realism\, and surrealism\, drawi
 ng inspiration from human emotion\, urban solitude\, connection\, memorie
 s\, nature\, and time.\nHer series\,\nPassage of Time\n\, reflects her exp
 eriences of city life and explores themes of contrast and contradiction—
  visual beauty paired with melancholy\, and relaxation alongside lonelines
 s\, much like life itself\, where joy and sorrow coexist. Her work often c
 arries hidden messages through symbolic elements.\nSine's work has been fe
 atured in various group exhibitions\, including at the Marianne van Silfho
 ut Gallery.\nThis exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibit Space\nprogram. To
 ronto Public Library provides space for local artists to exhibit their wor
 k at locations across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse 
 cultural interests of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be
  viewed during the Forest Hill branch's open hours. Please check the\nFore
 st Hill\nbranch page before you visit.\nFree. All are welcome.\nImage cred
 it: Sine Lam\; "Back to Silence"\; oil.
LOCATION:Forest Hill
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a80ca5ebe1482002987994a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
