BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AI for School: Responsible Success for Teens
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T180000
UID:6a9b4e3d3b6c71003e5de731@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:AI can help with schoolwork. So why does it feel like walking 
 a tightrope? How do you use it for learning without fooling yourself?\nIn 
 this youth-focused class with our Innovator-in-Residence\,\nRyan Kelln\n\,
  you'll learn to use AI as a tutor\, quiz partner\, and explainer\, not an
  answer machine. You'll practice the tutor loop using provided examples: s
 tarting with what your interests are\, what you want to learn\, how you li
 ke to learn\, and what you already understand. We'll also cover academic p
 olicies around AI and when AI is the wrong tool entirely.\nPrerequisites:
  Mouse\, keyboarding and internet skills. Computers are provided. No co
 ding experience required.\nRegistration is required and will start Septemb
 er 9\, 2026 at 9:00 AM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed after 5 mi
 nutes of the start of the program.\nAfter this time\, remaining seats will
  be filled on a first come\, first serve basis until capacity is reached.
  If you wish to save your work from this hands-on program\, please bring 
 your own USB stick.\nAbout the AI Tools Used in This Program\nThis program
  includes activities that use agentic AI tools (listed below) on library l
 aptops.\nYou do not need to create your own account for this program.\nPar
 ticipants are encouraged to follow the Resident’s guidance throughout se
 ssions\, which include best practices on using AI.\nWe encourage you to re
 view the privacy statements of each tool prior to attending this program:\
 nClaude Code\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle Ant
 igravity\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle AI Stud
 io\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nInformation Collecti
 on Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toro
 nto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)
 \, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regi
 stration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handle
 s your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.
 ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b4e3d3b6c71003e5de731
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
