UID:6abc169be8cf1c005cafe983@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:New to Scarborough? This three-session series is designed for 
 you. Learn how to find local services and community resources online\, bui
 ld a personal map of your neighbourhood\, and create something you can sha
 re with family and friends. Sessions are welcoming\, hands-on\, and delive
 red in plain language. No prior tech experience required\, just bring your
  questions. This is session one in a series\, separate registration requi
 red for each session\nArrive 30 minutes before or stay 30 minutes after th
 e program for one-on-one consultations.\nThis program is part of TPL's Inn
 ovator in Residence series focused on civic innovation. From October 5 to 
 November 28\, join programs\, workshops and one-on-one consultations led b
 y technology strategist Ismail Mohamud to learn how technology can help yo
 u create positive change in your community. Learn more at\ntpl.ca/iir\n.\n
 Information Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is c
 ollected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, se
 ctions 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for ev
 ent and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about ho
 w the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff
  at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4
 W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Second floor\, Digital Innovation Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abc169be8cf1c005cafe983
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
