BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AI for School: Responsible Success for Teens
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261013T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261013T180000
UID:6a9b4e1c1c197d11325d6f1b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:AI can help with schoolwork. So why does it feel like walking 
 a tightrope? How do you use it for learning without fooling yourself?\nIn 
 this youth-focused class\, you'll learn to use AI with our Innovator-in-R
 esidence\,\nRyan Kelln\n\, as a tutor\, quiz partner\, and explainer\, no
 t an answer machine. You'll practice the tutor loop using provided example
 s: starting with what your interests are\, what you want to learn\, how yo
 u like to learn\, and what you already understand. We'll also cover academ
 ic policies around AI and when AI is the wrong tool entirely.\nPrerequisit
 es: Mouse\, keyboarding and internet skills. Computers are provided. No
  coding experience required.\nRegistration is required and will start Sept
 ember 9\, 2026 at 9:00 AM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed after 5
  minutes of the start of the program.\nAfter this time\, remaining seats w
 ill be filled on a first come\, first serve basis until capacity is reache
 d. If you wish to save your work from this hands-on program\, please brin
 g your own USB stick.\nAbout the AI Tools Used in This Program\nThis progr
 am includes activities that use agentic AI tools (listed below) on library
  laptops.\nYou do not need to create your own account for this program.\nP
 articipants are encouraged to follow the Resident’s guidance throughout 
 sessions\, which include best practices on using AI.\nWe encourage you to 
 review the privacy statements of each tool prior to attending this program
 :\nClaude Code\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle A
 ntigravity\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle AI St
 udio\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nInformation Collec
 tion Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the To
 ronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(
 c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program re
 gistration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library hand
 les your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tp
 l.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b4e1c1c197d11325d6f1b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
