 y be available from library staff.\nThis program is part of Youth Hub serv
 ice. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teens after school and in the su
 mmer\, where helpful staff are always available. Free\, nutritious snacks
  are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branc
 h to find out more.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, Youth Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa185f0ca248a0029148e7e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pape Avenue After Dark: A Halloween History Walk - FULL
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261020T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261020T193000
UID:6aa990e8ab7a8e0037c1ffe2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join local history expert Harley Karulis as we take a\nHallowe
 en history walk along\nPape Avenue\n\, where the familiar neighborhood tak
 es on a whole new personality after the sun goes down. We will uncover th
 e people\, places\, and stories that helped shape this fascinating part of
  Toronto\, along with some of the darker\, and downright creepy tales that
  history sometimes prefers to keep hidden. Bring your curiosity\, and mayb
 e a little courage!\nWe will begin at the Pape Public Library and make our
  way along Pape Avenue\, returning to the library. Remember to wear your 
 walking shoes!\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information o
 n this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Li
 braries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will onl
 y be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Qu
 estions about how the library handles your information can be directed to 
 Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street
 \, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Pape/Danforth\, Ground floor.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa990e8ab7a8e0037c1ffe2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:FRESH Movie Saturdays
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261219T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261219T130000
UID:6ac7f0c229c3d600332e9eb0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn n
 ew skills\, and have fun. Meet new folks\, build connections\, and tell us
  about programs and services you would like to see in the neighbourhood!\n
 Come join us every Saturday for screenings of your favourite movies. In ad
 dition to this\, enjoy cuddles with a therapy dog! Therapy dog Goose visi
 ts Fort York Branch on alternate Saturdays from 11:00AM-12:00PM.\nWe'll b
 e showing the following films:\nOct 3 - The Shaggy Dog (1959)\nOct 10 - Pl
 anes\, Trains and Automobiles\nOct 17 - Toy Story 5\nOct 24 - The Absent M
 inded Professor (1961)\nOct 31 - Hotel Transylvania\nNov 7 - Herbie the L
 ove Bug (1968)\nNov 14 - Africa-An Cats\nNov 21 - The Odd Life of Timothy 
 Green\nNov 28 - Little Big League\nDec 5 – Dog Man\nDec 12 – Toy Stor
 y 5\nDec 19 - A Muppet Christmas Carol\nDrop-ins are welcome.\nThis progra
 m is in collaboration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's F.R.E.S.H. initiative
 \n.
LOCATION:Fort York\, Urban Living Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac7f0c229c3d600332e9eb0
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
