BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tutankhamun: The Sensational Discovery - Part 1
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261014T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261014T193000
UID:6aad8cc6b19bb10d7c331cb3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This year marks an important anniversary in the history of Egy
 ptology. On November 4th\, 2026\, it will be 104 years since Howard Carter
  and Lord Carnarvon discovered the intact tomb of King Tutankhamun in 1922
  - a discovery that continues to capture the public imagination.\nNearly a
  year after the complete collection went on display at the Grand Egyptian 
 Museum in Cairo on November 1\, 2025\, Sherine ElSebaie will take audience
 s back to the moment of its discovery. Following the footsteps of the exca
 vators\, she will recount the story leading to the discovery of the tomb a
 nd explore the remarkable objects found in its first two chambers during t
 he initial excavation in 1922.\nSherine ElSebaie is an Egyptologist who be
 gan her academic journey with a B.Sc. in Egypt\, completed a Master’s de
 gree in Egyptology at the University of Toronto. She then engaged in advan
 ced doctoral studies\, further deepening her expertise in the field. She s
 pecializes in ancient Egyptian art and religion\, with particular interest
 s in the history of archeology\, tourism\, and cultural heritage.\nRegistr
 ation is encouraged but not required.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe
  personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Libr
 ary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). T
 he information will only be used for event and program registration\, deli
 very and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informat
 ion can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-
 5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 1 (2nd floor)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aad8cc6b19bb10d7c331cb3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
