BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Newcomers Civic Track: 3
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T200000
UID:6abc216511bbf300684a75fc@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:New to Scarborough? This three-session series is designed for 
 you. Learn how to find local services and community resources online\, bui
 ld a personal map of your neighbourhood\, and create something you can sha
 re with family and friends. Sessions are welcoming\, hands-on\, and delive
 red in plain language. No prior tech experience required\, just bring your
  questions. This is session three in a series\, separate registration req
 uired for each session.\nArrive 30 minutes before or stay 30 minutes after
  the program for one-on-one consultations.\nThis program is part of TPL's 
 Innovator in Residence series focused on civic innovation. From October 5 
 to November 28\, join programs\, workshops and one-on-one consultations le
 d by technology strategist Ismail Mohamud to learn how technology can help
  you create positive change in your community. Learn more at\ntpl.ca/iir\n
 .\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form i
 s collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\,
  sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for
  event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about
  how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline st
 aff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON
  M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Second floor\, Digital Innovation Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abc216511bbf300684a75fc
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
