BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Orientation Intensive
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261016T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261016T200000
UID:6a9c776329a7dd0d674955dd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Missed one of our orientation sessions? This single session br
 ings together everything from the first three: an introduction to civic in
 novation and the Civix by Design program\, a walkthrough of Toronto Open D
 ata and public datasets\, and a hands-on tour of the tools we will use. It
  is a fast-paced overview designed to get you fully caught up and ready to
  participate in any session in the series.\nArrive 30 minutes before or st
 ay 30 minutes after the program for one-on-one consultations.\nThis progra
 m is part of TPL's Innovator in Residence series focused on civic innovati
 on. From October 5 to November 28\, join programs\, workshops and one-on-o
 ne consultations led by technology strategist Ismail Mohamud to learn how 
 technology can help you create positive change in your community. Learn mo
 re at\ntpl.ca/iir\n.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal informa
 tion on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Pub
 lic Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information wi
 ll only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluati
 on. Questions about how the library handles your information can be direct
 ed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge 
 Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Small Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9c776329a7dd0d674955dd
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
