BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branding for Youth Adults: A YMCA Youth for Entrepreneurship Works
 hop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261102T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261102T190000
UID:6aaa95e0101eb7003f3083f9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Find your brand identity\, how digital marketing works\, and h
 ow it can help young entrepreneurs like you! Learn about the different typ
 es of social media and which to utilize for your business. You will leave 
 this session with some fantastic free resources to get you started!\nRegis
 tration required. Limited spots. Young Adults (ages 18-24) have priority f
 or this workshop.\nThis program will be taking place in\nLearning Centre 2
 \n\,\nlocated on the first floor (in between the TD Gallery and the book s
 tore).\n----\nThis workshop is part of the Youth for Entrepreneurship prog
 ram led by the YMCA of Greater Toronto. Through hands-on sessions\, you’
 ll gain the digital tools\, financial knowledge\, and creative strategies 
 needed to build a business idea from the ground up.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Learning Centre 2 (1st Floor)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaa95e0101eb7003f3083f9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Artists in the Library: Origami Lotus Flowers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261211T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261211T180000
UID:6aac152519094f0c6938b75b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This is a six-part workshop series that creates a space for ex
 ploring belonging and not belonging through conversation and hands-on art-
 making. Guided by reflective questions\, participants engage in practices 
 such as origami with washi\, drawing\, dyeing\, and writing\, using the lo
 tus as a shared symbol of transformation and resilience across cultures. T
 he workshops foster an inclusive\, supportive environment\, particularly f
 or those who feel marginalized or disconnected. The series culminates in a
  collaborative public floral installation in the library\, sharing partici
 pants’ work with the wider community.\nLed by artists "Being~inbetween"\
 nThe workshops are open to youth\, ages 13-17\, and require no prior artis
 tic experience.\nWorkshop Dates:\nFriday\, September 11th\nFriday\, Septem
 ber 18th\nFriday\, October 30th\nFriday\, November 6th\nFriday\, December 
 4th\nFriday\, December 11th
LOCATION:Thorncliffe\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aac152519094f0c6938b75b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
