UID:6abe8972754bb0003ac29745@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this hands-on session\, you will design and 3D print a phys
 ical response to a civic challenge then explain the thinking behind what y
 ou built. From concept to object\, you will learn the basics of 3D design 
 and discover how making something tangible can sharpen your civic ideas. N
 o design experience required.\nArrive 30 minutes before or stay 30 minutes
  after the program for one-on-one consultations.\nThis program is part of 
 TPL's Innovator in Residence series focused on civic innovation. From Octo
 ber 5 to November 28\, join programs\, workshops and one-on-one consultati
 ons led by technology strategist Ismail Mohamud to learn how technology ca
 n help you create positive change in your community. Learn more at\ntpl.ca
 /iir\n.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this 
 form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries
  Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be us
 ed for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions
  about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerl
 ine staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toro
 nto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Second Floor\, Digital Innovation Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abe8972754bb0003ac29745
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
