BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Why We Misunderstand the Middle East and Why it Matters
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T200000
UID:6aa082354cb69d003e26ac5e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Participants will gain a clearer\, more grounded understanding
  of how common misconceptions about the Middle East are formed and why the
 y persist. They will learn to recognize how media narratives\, language\, 
 and framing shape interpretation\, often in subtle ways.\nThe session will
  offer practical tools for questioning familiar assumptions\, evaluating i
 nformation more critically\, and approaching discussions about the region 
 with greater nuance and context. Participants will also gain a broader app
 reciation of the historical\, cultural\, linguistic\, and political divers
 ity that exists within the Middle East\, helping them move beyond simplifi
 ed understandings.\nPresented by Dr. Hamid Yazdi
LOCATION:St. Lawrence\, Ground Floor\, South Side
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa082354cb69d003e26ac5e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
