UID:6abc20d211bbf300684a75f2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:New to Scarborough? This three-session series is designed for 
 you. Learn how to find local services and community resources online\, bui
 ld a personal map of your neighbourhood\, and create something you can sha
 re with family and friends. Sessions are welcoming\, hands-on\, and delive
 red in plain language. No prior tech experience required\, just bring your
  questions. This is session two in a series\, separate registration requi
 red for each session.\nArrive 30 minutes before or stay 30 minutes after t
 he program for one-on-one consultations.\nThis program is part of TPL's In
 novator in Residence series focused on civic innovation. From October 5 to
  November 28\, join programs\, workshops and one-on-one consultations led 
 by technology strategist Ismail Mohamud to learn how technology can help y
 ou create positive change in your community. Learn more at\ntpl.ca/iir\n.\
 nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is 
 collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, s
 ections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for e
 vent and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about h
 ow the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staf
 f at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M
 4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Second floor\, Digital Innovation Hub
