BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Kensington Market: Heart of the City -  Documentary Screening Pres
 ented by Producer and Director Stuart Clarfield
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T200000
UID:6ac1469929c3d600332d6db7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Kensington Market\nStuart Clarfield's feature documentary expl
 ores Kensington Market's 160-year history\, from it origins as a Victorian
  suburb of Toronto\, to its roots as a Jewish immigrant marketplace to its
  evolution as a cultural hub for almost every community that calls Toronto
  home. The film highlights the neighbourhood's vibrant identity and its on
 going struggle against gentrification and development\, attempting to pres
 erve the rich bohemian spirit of Kensington\, as modern Toronto grows arou
 nd it. 104 minutes (2024).\nOnline registration is optional\, not required
 .\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form i
 s collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\,
  sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for
  event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about
  how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline st
 aff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON
  M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium (2nd floor)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac1469929c3d600332d6db7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
