BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Writings of David Thompson on His Travels in North America
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261111T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261111T183000
UID:6ab2b15eed69cc15475c1139@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Writings of David Thompson\nThis presentation examines the
  historical Writings of David Thompson. Between 1784 and 1812\, David Thom
 pson (1770-1857) explored and traded over a vast expanse of western North 
 America. Later in life\, the surveyor and fur trader wrote what he called 
 his\nTravels\n\, a spectacular geographical and spirited intellectual jour
 ney of the Canadian experience. His story tells of a remarkable life in th
 e fur trade but it also captures hid reflections on the land and the indig
 enous peoples of western North America.\nPresented by Bill Moreau\, editor
  of the three-volume work\,\nThe Writings of David Thompson\n.\nRegistrati
 on is encouraged but not necessary.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe p
 ersonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Librar
 y under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The
  information will only be used for event and program registration\, delive
 ry and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informatio
 n can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-59
 81\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 1\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab2b15eed69cc15475c1139
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
