BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:"Make It Heard" 2: Civic Problem-Solving & Digital Advocacy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T200000
UID:6a9c78b7be148200298cc959@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Every community has problems. This series gives you the tools 
 to do something about them. Over three sessions you will define a real civ
 ic challenge in your neighbourhood\, design a creative response\, and buil
 d something: a digital campaign\, a poster\, a video pitch\, or even a 3D-
 printed prototype that communicates your idea to the public. Come ready to
  think\, build\, and be heard.\nArrive 30 minutes before or stay 30 minute
 s after the program for one-on-one consultations.\nThis program is part of
  TPL's Innovator in Residence series focused on civic innovation. From Oct
 ober 5 to November 28\, join programs\, workshops and one-on-one consultat
 ions led by technology strategist Ismail Mohamud to learn how technology c
 an help you create positive change in your community. Learn more at\ntpl.c
 a/iir\n.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this
  form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Librarie
 s Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be u
 sed for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Question
 s about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answer
 line staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Tor
 onto ON M4W 2G8
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Digital Innovation Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9c78b7be148200298cc959
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: DJ At Any Age: Introduction to DJing Learning Series
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261109T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261109T180000
UID:6aa1b2d58cf597003f925244@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:During this comprehensive 4-week course​\, participants lear
 n essential deejaying skills such as song selection and mixing\, working w
 ith volume and tempo\, understanding deejay terminology\, and using effect
 s and samples. ​ Led by Deejay Vee.\nParticipants will understand how to
  use a dj controller (i.e. deck\, mixer and effects sections) ​​\nPart
 icipants will understand how to use djing software (i.e. using crates\, cr
 eating playlist\, setting cue points\, etc.)\nParticipants can use their n
 ew deejaying skills to curate an awesome musical experience.\nThis program
  is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teens 
 after school and in the summer\, where helpful staff are always available.
  Free\, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\nYo
 uth Hub\nor call the branch to find out more.\nInformation Collection Noti
 ce:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Pub
 lic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 
 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registratio
 n\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your 
 information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 
 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Auditorium (lower level)
