BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Exploring Mindfulness Through Art with Michelle Bancrof
 t
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261109T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261109T173000
UID:6ac9347f901b02002cc14134@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for Mindfulness Through Art with Michelle Bancroft!\nE
 xplore simple mindfulness tools that can help with stress\, anxiety\, and 
 feeling overwhelmed. Create your own Mindfulness Jar to see what the mind 
 can feel like when thoughts are racing and learn easy breathing and ground
 ing techniques that can help bring a sense of calm and focus. You'll also 
 take part in a colouring activity that helps you identify where emotions s
 how up in your body and discover how mindfulness can help you feel more pr
 esent\, balanced\, and connected.\nNo art skills or mindfulness experience
  needed\, just come ready to relax\, create\, and try something new!\nThis
  program is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place fo
 r teens after school and in the summer\, where helpful staff are always av
 ailable. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch wi
 th a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to find out more.
LOCATION:Eatonville
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac9347f901b02002cc14134
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
