BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Transforming Garbage - Make a Monster Plushie
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T180000
UID:6a90686a57c264087ad4354e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What is “garbage”? How do we define what materials can be 
 reused? The answer to these questions rely on an investigation of imaginat
 ion. Any material can be reused to create art.\nMonster’s pre-date the w
 ritten word\, making them crucial to storytelling and to the development 
 of shared history. In this workshop\, we will delve into creative express
 ion and storytelling as we build a Monster Plushie together. Through guide
 d instructions and with donated fabrics\, participants will learn the bas
 ics of sewing and pattern making.\nThis program is part of Youth Hub serv
 ice. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teens after school and in the su
 mmer\, where helpful staff are always available. Free\, nutritious snacks
  are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branc
 h to find out more.
LOCATION:Parliament Street\, 2nd Floor Youth Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a90686a57c264087ad4354e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Cupcake Decorating
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T170000
UID:6a90697257c264087ad4355c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Pastry Chef Yumiko Kobayashi leads this hands-on one-hour cupc
 ake workshop where participants will each mix icing\, pipe\, and decorate 
 two cupcakes. Participants will learn primary techniques like piping with 
 cream cheese and buttercream frosting and decorating. All ingredients to b
 e provided and prepped by the chef.\nFood allergy notice: Please be aware 
 that food will be used in this program that contains gluten and dairy.  Ce
 rtain food ingredients may cause allergic reactions in some people.\nThis 
 program is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for
  teens after school and in the summer\, where helpful staff are always ava
 ilable. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch wit
 h a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to find out more.
LOCATION:Parliament Street\, 2nd Floor Youth Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a90697257c264087ad4355c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
