BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tutankhamun: The Sensational Discovery - Part 2
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T193000
UID:6aaedabbca248a002916fe35@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This year marks an important anniversary in the history of Egy
 ptology. On November 4th\, 2026\, it will be 104 years since Howard Carter
  and Lord Carnarvon discovered the intact tomb of King Tutankhamun in 1922
  - a discovery that continues to capture the public imagination.\nNearly a
  year after the complete collection went on display at the Grand Egyptian 
 Museum in Cairo on November 1\, 2025\, Egyptologist Sherine ElSebaie will 
 take audiences back to the time of its discovery. Following the footsteps 
 of the excavators\, she will conclude the story of the discovery and explo
 re the remarkable objects found in the burial chamber and the treasury dur
 ing the excavation of 1923.\nRegistration is encouraged but not required.\
 nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is 
 collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, s
 ections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for e
 vent and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about h
 ow the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staf
 f at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M
