DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261026T183000
UID:6ab15fdc86d845003117b1ff@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Adobe Premiere is the industry-leading video editing software.
  In this introductory class you will learn basic video editing techniques.
 \nWith this powerful tool\, you can edit virtually any type of media creat
 e professional productions for film\, TV and the web.  Premiere is a time-
 line based video editing application and can also integrate with the rest 
 of the Adobe suite such as After Effects\, Photoshop and more.\nIn this in
 troductory Premiere class you will learn basic video editing techniques su
 ch as adding clips\, transitions and titles.  Add audio to your project\, 
 along with cutting and splicing on your project’s timeline.\nAges 13+\nR
 egistration is required for this class.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nT
 he personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Li
 brary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d).
  The information will only be used for event and program registration\, de
 livery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your inform
 ation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-39
 7-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Downsview
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab15fdc86d845003117b1ff
