DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261019T120000
UID:6ab6a0b6a5dbde002aa7262f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a series of group workshops for anyone navigating 
 relationships\, caregiving responsibilities or family dynamics. Explore th
 e impact these experiences can have on mental health and well-being\, lear
 n practical strategies\, and connect with others in a supportive\, non-jud
 gmental environment. Some workshops are co-facilitated by CMHA Toronto’s
  Family Support Team\, bringing together professional expertise and lived 
 experience to support honest\, practical and compassionate conversations.\
 nRegistration is required.\nTTC Presto tickets will be provided upon reque
 st.\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredient
  lists will be available at the program.\nThis program is in collaborati
 on with\nCanadian Mental Health Association Toronto.\nInformation Collecti
 on Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toro
 nto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)
 \, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regi
 stration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handle
 s your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.
 ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Room 201\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab6a0b6a5dbde002aa7262f
